NAME
    resume - resume emulation after an interactive halt

SYNOPSIS
    resume
    c

DESCRIPTION
    Signals the attached emulation session to resume running after a
    breakpoint, single-step, run-to event, or interactive debug halt.

    'c' is registered by the emusen.trace module as a direct alias for
    'resume'. When invoked outside any shell loop, the shell keyword
    continue(1) also resumes emulation (inside a 'for' or 'while' loop it
    advances the loop instead).

EXAMPLES
    resume
    c

EXIT STATUS
    0   Resume request issued.
    1   Session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    continue(1), step(1), runto(1), bp(1)
